<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H17212</pnldref><english><title>Aid / abet / assist in fraudulent fixing / placing of a stamp on stamp / cut / torn / removed from a stamp / material</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>aided</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>abetted</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>assisted</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>fraud</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>fraudulently</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>placed</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>cutted</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>tear</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>tore</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>remove</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..) knowingly aided, abetted or assisted **(..SPECIFY PERSON..) to fraudulently fix or place upon &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;(A)_[material]_&lt;br /&gt;(B)_[a stamp]_&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;a stamp or part of a stamp which had been cut, torn, or removed from other material, or out of or from another stamp</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to section 13(1), (2) and (6) of the Stamp Duties Management Act 1891.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt;knowingly aided/abetted/assisted in the &lt;br /&gt;fraudulent&lt;br /&gt;fixing/placing upon material/a stamp&lt;br /&gt;a stamp/part of a stamp which&lt;br /&gt;whether fraudulently or not&lt;br /&gt;was cut/torn/removed&lt;br /&gt;from any other material/out of/from another stamp</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA6</code><description>Offences brought to justice scheme</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>EWAY</code><description>EITHER WAY</description></modeoftrial><timelimitforprosecutions>None</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>Summary: Six months imprisonment and / or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.&lt;br /&gt;Indictment: Ten years imprisonment and / or a fine.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Time limit for prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt;None&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;On the 12th March 2015 the limit on fines imposed by a Magistrates' court was removed – as such, the potential fine on summary conviction in relation to an offence committed after this date is unlimited.</penalty><geographicregion><code>EW</code><description>England and Wales</description></geographicregion></other><codes><cjsoffencecode>SD91014</cjsoffencecode><recordableonpncindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></recordableonpncindicator><pncacpooffencecode>4.1.88.1</pncacpooffencecode><notifiabletoho><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></notifiabletoho><hoclassification>053/11</hoclassification><mopireviewgroup><code>C</code><description>Group 3</description></mopireviewgroup><mopinoteslink>D19586</mopinoteslink><seatbeltoffence><code>N</code><description>No</description></seatbeltoffence><fptissuedbypolice>0</fptissuedbypolice><fptgraduated>0</fptgraduated><fptgraduatedhigh>0</fptgraduatedhigh><pndissuedbypolice>0</pndissuedbypolice><pndissuedbylocalauthorities>0</pndissuedbylocalauthorities><pndissuedbyothers>0</pndissuedbyothers><roadsidedeposits><code>N</code><description>No</description></roadsidedeposits></codes><libra><cjsoffencecategory><code>CE</code><description>Either Way</description></cjsoffencecategory><fineindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></fineindicator><maxfinetypemagct><code>U</code><description>Unlimited</description></maxfinetypemagct><maxfinetypecrownct><code>U</code><description>Unlimited</description></maxfinetypecrownct><custodialindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></custodialindicator><maxcustodialsentenceunitmagct><code>Months</code><description>Months</description></maxcustodialsentenceunitmagct><maxcustodialsentencelengthmagct>6</maxcustodialsentencelengthmagct><maxcustodialsentenceunitcrownct><code>Years</code><description>Years</description></maxcustodialsentenceunitcrownct><maxcustodialsentencelengthcrownct>10</maxcustodialsentencelengthcrownct><miscode><code>FRF</code><description>Fraud and Forgery</description></miscode></libra><ancillary><offencestartdate>1999-10-01</offencestartdate><datecreated>2011-01-31</datecreated><auditofamend